F-0056 hook patch, written by Smith 26 Oct 2026 20:15. Not applied: a scheduled run cannot edit the hook.

Why: on 25 Oct 2026 the nightly's third spawn was denied "4 of 4 already used" after 2 allows. BST
ended at 01:00 that morning, so at 23:31 GMT `time.time() - 86400` was 23:31 GMT on 24 Oct, which is
00:31 BST on 25 Oct: "yesterday" and "today" were the same date, the 25 Oct decisions log was read
twice and every allow counted double. Same fault doubles the daily ceiling count for that hour each
autumn, and in spring (00:30 BST on 30 Mar 2026) it reads 28 and 30 Mar, skipping the real yesterday. The patch steps back one calendar day (noon, via mktime) instead of 86,400 seconds.

Proof without the hook: python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0056-check.py
(old way reads 2026-10-25 twice on the night; patched way gives two distinct dates on six instants,
both DST edges, month and year edges).

Apply from an interactive session:
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply --check /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0056.diff
  git -C /Users/triton/PROTEUS apply /Users/triton/PROTEUS/state/loop/hook-patches/F-0056.diff
  python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/test-hook.py        (no new cases: the bug lives in date arithmetic, see the check script)
and close: python3 /Users/triton/PROTEUS/bin/findings.py fix F-0056 --commit <hash> --note 'spawn counter steps back a calendar day; DST double read gone'
Line numbers are against 93714ab (26 Oct).

--- a/.claude/hooks/unattended-decide.py
+++ b/.claude/hooks/unattended-decide.py
